# A flowing mountain sprint. Distances are metres; angles are degrees.
name "Ridgeway Pass"
description "Climb a broad ridge, thread narrowing switchbacks, and sweep back down to the valley."
width 14

# A heading of -40 points northwest instead of along the default +Z axis.
start -180 12 80 -40
kind road
straight 150 rise 12

# Split the corner so its bank builds, holds through the middle, then unwinds.
right 20 radius 85 rise 3 bank -14
right 60 radius 85 rise 12
right 20 radius 85 rise 3 bank 0
checkpoint

# Width changes blend across the next command: the ascent tightens to 11 m.
width 11
straight 100 rise 20
left 20 radius 75 rise 2 bank 16
left 70 radius 75 rise 8
left 20 radius 75 rise 2 bank 0
straight 110 rise 8
checkpoint

# The summit is 70 m above the start. Negative rise begins the descent.
# Widen through the first downhill corner to leave room for braking.
width 13
right 20 radius 90 rise -3 bank -14
right 70 radius 90 rise -12
right 20 radius 90 rise -3 bank 0
straight 130 rise -20
checkpoint

# A final sweeping bend leads to a wide, level-bank run to the finish.
left 20 radius 90 rise -3 bank 14
left 60 radius 90 rise -12
left 20 radius 90 rise -3 bank 0
width 14
straight 200 rise -14
finish
